 "purpose": "The topics of fractions: recognising and shading on the fraction bar, equivalent and simplifying, comparing, adding and subtracting, a fraction of a number (and x and :), and fraction versus decimal.",
 "details": "Six Onderwerp subclasses sharing a base _Breuken (cheat sheet, repetition group from the key, choice of the question kind from the leerlijn, and the 'correct but not simplified' hint). Answers are exact Fractions; a typed fraction is read as GetypteBreuk so the form counts where the question demands the simplest form (data['vereenvoudigd']). Several topics attach a visual model that is shown only after checking (model_na, such as fraction bars with a common denominator from balken_gelijknamig). Optellen and BreukVan have a worked solution in klad lines (oplossing). Used by Wiskunde > Breuken en procenten. A related plan to show fractions stacked (teller above noemer) is parked in werk/breuken.md and is not in this code.",
 "module_docstring": "Breuken: herkennen en arceren op de breukbalk, gelijkwaardig en vereenvoudigen, vergelijken, optellen en aftrekken, een breuk van een getal (en vermenigvuldigen/delen), breuk en kommagetal.",
